  table  -> /root/rna_work_r/results/tables/18_power_by_alpha.tsv

Power at a twofold change, median gene, 4 replicates per group:
  upper bound (no correction):  0.846
  lower bound (Bonferroni):     0.128

The lower bound is far below 0.8, and the real figure for an FDR procedure lies somewhere between the two. The power of this
experiment to detect a twofold change in a typical gene is therefore NOT ESTABLISHED, and it is poor for the more variable
genes whichever end is taken. The near-empty result for this contrast cannot be read as evidence of no change over time, and
the 2 genes found cannot be read as a finding either. Both are what an experiment this size can produce with or without an effect.
This is power at a twofold change only; a smaller true change is not excluded by any of these numbers.

=== would more sequencing have helped? ===
  depth     133 counts -> power 0.846
  depth     266 counts -> power 0.858
  depth    1330 counts -> power 0.868
  depth   13300 counts -> power 0.870
Depth saturates: within-group variability and sample size are what bind here, exactly as the lecture's four levers predict.

